The post-hook [Hook feedback] block now has a test that checks the request actually sent to the model, not just the result the hook wrapper returns. It's committed as be3869a4 with the title "Part of #1054", and the full gate passed: fmt, clippy -D warnings, build, and the whole cargo test.

One correction to the plan. The task wanted the feedback checked as its own text block in the request. That can't be seen on the Anthropic wire: yoagent sends a text-only tool result as one string, joining the blocks with "\n" (provider::tool_result_text). The block list only appears when an image is in the result. So the test checks the exact form that does go out: the hooked result must equal the hook-free run's result, plus "\n", plus "\n[Hook feedback]\nHOOKMARK-7731". Taking the start of that string from a second run with no hook keeps the test independent of bash's output format, and it still proves three things: the tool's output is unchanged, the feedback arrives, and it comes after the output rather than mixed into it.

What changed:
• `tests/hook_feedback_request.rs` (new). It runs the built binary against a stub provider that records each request. The stub's first reply asks for a bash tool call (echo hi). The hook is set as hooks.post.bash in the project's .yoyo.toml and loaded with --trust-project. My first attempt, a [hooks] table, loaded nothing. The fixture uses its own temp HOME and the same key-scrubbing as sub_agent_usage_record.rs. A second test runs with no hook and checks there's no [Hook feedback] text and no marker anywhere.
• Positive control. I disabled the feedback push in one command (marked NEUTERED), ran the tests, then restored it. Only the new presence test failed, at the assert_eq on line 318; the no-hook test stayed green. After restoring, src/hooks.rs matches HEAD exactly, no markers are left, and both tests pass.
• Docs. I added a comment at the push site in src/hooks.rs with a yoagent-version-claim: 0.25 marker (doc_version_claims passes), and one sentence to the hooks.rs entry in ARCHITECTURE.md.

Left open on #1054 (in the commit body and in a comment on the issue):
